# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own values.
# .env is git-ignored — never commit real keys.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED — your Etsy app credentials (BOTH halves)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create an app at https://www.etsy.com/developers/your-apps
# Etsy shows a "Keystring" and a "Shared secret". You need BOTH.
#
# Every v3 request must carry them colon-joined in the x-api-key header, even the
# unauthenticated ones. With the keystring alone Etsy replies:
#   403 {"error":"Invalid API key: should be in the format 'keystring:shared_secret'."}
#
# This is separate from OAuth. PKCE removes the client secret from the token
# exchange (client_id is the bare keystring) — it does not remove the shared
# secret from the x-api-key header. etsyotomasyon joins them for you.
ETSY_KEYSTRING=
ETSY_SHARED_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED for `etsyotomasyon auth login` — your OAuth callback
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Must match a callback URL registered on your Etsy app, byte for byte.
# Etsy's app settings screen states the rules:
#   - must start with http:// or https://
#   - the host must be a domain name (e.g. example.com)
#   - IP addresses are NOT allowed (e.g. 127.0.0.1)
#
# 'localhost' is a domain name, so a local callback is fine and is the easiest
# option: etsyotomasyon starts a one-shot listener on that port and catches the code
# for you, with nothing to copy. Register this same string on your app:
ETSY_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3003/oauth/redirect
#
# If you use any other host, Etsy redirects your browser there and you paste the
# address back into etsyotomasyon once. That page does not need to exist or serve
# anything — the authorization code is in the address bar.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Only needed if your Etsy account owns more than one shop, or you want to be
# explicit. Otherwise etsyotomasyon discovers it from the authenticated user.
# ETSY_SHOP_ID=

# Space-separated OAuth scopes. The default is the minimum etsyotomasyon needs.
# Narrow it further if you only want read access:
#   ETSY_SCOPES=shops_r listings_r transactions_r
# ETSY_SCOPES=shops_r listings_r listings_w transactions_r transactions_w

# Requests per second. Limits are PER APP and printed on your app's row at
# etsy.com/developers/your-apps. A Personal Access app gets 5 QPS / 5,000 per day.
# The default of 4 stays under that. Raise it only if your app shows a higher
# allowance — the 10/sec figure in Etsy's general docs is the commercial tier.
# ETSYOTOMASYON_RATE_PER_SEC=4

# Where tokens and cache are stored. Defaults to ~/.etsyotomasyon
# ETSYOTOMASYON_HOME=

# --- Pinterest (optional) ---------------------------------------------------
# Only needed for `etsyotomasyon pinterest`. Create your own app at
# https://developers.pinterest.com/apps/ and register the redirect URI below on it.
# PINTEREST_APP_ID=
# PINTEREST_APP_SECRET=
# PINTEREST_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8085/
# Trial-access apps may only write to the sandbox, which takes a token generated in
# the developer portal instead of `etsyotomasyon pinterest login`.
# PINTEREST_SANDBOX=1
# PINTEREST_ACCESS_TOKEN=
